The minor in which a hub's members become reachable one by one, reasoning and change cross them, and a project can take reflow2's kit back out. It carries:
- #774: init --remove, and update never brings a removed kit back;
- #775 (P4a): `member` on every tool through a hub, prefixed ids in every routed reply, an id naming a member routes every tool;
- #776 (P4b): a far premise reads its live truth (stale/unreachable), propagate continues into view members holding an xref, the no-export line names .reflow2.toml first, delete_node by bare id;
- the cut itself (release/v0.89.0).

Pinned here: rel:v0890, the increment's ChangeEvents (found by diffing ids against the v0.88.0 tag's committed copy, plus the live writes since), and the cut's drift acceptances.
